# 📚 What I Learned

Through creating this poster, I learned that good graphic design is not necessarily about adding more elements.

It is about knowing **which elements deserve attention**.

Minimalism taught me that empty space can be just as important as an image, and that a simple color palette can create a strong visual identity.

I also learned that advertisements can communicate emotions, not just information.

A coffee poster can make people think about warmth, comfort, energy, friendship, and good memories — all without using a complicated design.

